"""Prepare nine distinct geography-bound background generation briefs."""
import json, importlib.util
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
OUT=ROOT/'docs/美术规范/百川九张底图_20261027';(OUT/'引导').mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('guides',ROOT/'tools/world_map/plan_bai_chuan_nine_chunks_20261027.py');mod=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
d=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/prototypes/百川宗门城镇资源规划数据_20261027.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
briefs={
 '11':('西北源岭','Western upper watershed and mountain-front country. Low broken grey-olive ridges descend from the left and upper-left, opening toward the east and southeast. Several small SHALLOW tributary rills and moist grassy hollows gather eastward; this is an inhabited river-and-lake region, not a dry wasteland. No snow, desert or giant cliff wall. River corridors shown in blue are authoritative; little decorative feeder rills must remain thin and subordinate. Five future places need generous open foothill flats. Lower and right borders transition to valley land, not a closed enclosing mountain frame.'),
 '12':('北中台原','Northern gently raised terraces and open basins: low rounded ridges along the lower half and near upper corners, broad pale river-fed grassland and spring hollows between them. Sparse pine and broadleaf copses; understated wet soil ribbons, not a barren plateau or snowy north continent. Keep large clear flats for the northern city and main sect. The south edge opens toward the central basin and streams. Small winding feeder streams only; do not invent a large lake or draw a mountain fortress.'),
 '13':('东北河口','Northeastern river mouth and near-sea water country. Follow the guide main river: it enters the BOTTOM edge around x52%, bends toward x82% y75%, then exits the RIGHT edge around y72%. Quiet grey-blue water, alluvial sandbanks, narrow reed beds, little tidal inlets and moist flat shore. A restrained near-sea inlet touches the far right outer edge around the river mouth; inland to the left stays flat and usable. A few low dry ridges at the upper-left, sparse shore woods. Do not paint a harbor, boats, piers or buildings; leave open shore sites for separate landmarks. No huge ocean occupying the whole tile.'),
 '21':('西中溪岭','Western middle mountain-and-creek transition. Broken low ridge profiles along the western side, many valley gaps and moist woodland margins. A narrow watercourse begins around x75% y35% and exits the RIGHT edge around y38%, according to the guide; several small feeder rills in the western hollows give it an upstream catchment. The lower edge opens into southwest foothills, the right side opens into the central water valley. Dry grey-brown pen mountains with light olive wash, not sheer cliffs; keep pass openings and broad land for the local sect and river town.'),
 '22':('中央河湖','The central living basin of BAICHUAN, a region defined by connected rivers and lakes. It is NOT an empty desert square and NOT an island. Faithfully follow the blue guide centerline: main river enters LEFT edge near y38%, turns via x26% y29%, reaches confluence x53% y41%, bends via x74% y32%, exits RIGHT edge near y40%. A southwest tributary enters BOTTOM edge near x35%, climbs via x44% y77%, joins x53% y41%. A small irregular lake immediately below the confluence near x53% y48%, only about 10-14% tile width. Low grey-blue water, reed margins, a few moist sandbanks and intermittent sparse trees; occasional very low hill profiles near the top and bottom-left. At least 70% quiet usable land. No central clearing reserved for an alliance, no giant lake swallowing the cities.'),
 '23':('东中泽陵','Eastern middle region where the central river network meets low old hills. Main river enters LEFT edge near y38%, bends toward x22% y20%, exits TOP edge near x52%, as shown in the guide. A second smaller branch enters LEFT edge near y48%, runs down near x4% y68% toward x16% y95%, and exits BOTTOM near x17%. Keep these separate channels. Small still-water wetlands in the western/central part, grey-brown rounded hill profiles on the eastern side, scattered old trees and quiet broad land for an ancient temple city and the eastern great sect. Austere but natural, not deadlands, lava or black fantasy terrain.'),
 '31':('西南山前','Southwestern starting-country foothills. Layered modest grey-olive hills with broad valley floors, small clear springs and shallow creek traces feeding toward eastern river country. More gentle woodland margins than the northwest, with open flat ground at main-sect position around local x66% y22%. Quiet foothill flats for two cities and a few towns; no buildings or agricultural plot symbols. Top edge and right edge remain open, lower-left is low wooded hill country. Do not enclose the whole tile in an enormous mountain circle; let streams and valleys connect onward.'),
 '32':('南中林川','Southern middle wooded river valleys. The main visible tributary enters LEFT edge around y48%, curves via x17% y22%, exits TOP edge near x35%, matching the guide. Shallow grey-blue water, irregular banks, damp herb-like ground cover shown only as tiny vegetation marks, old woodland copses separated by generous clearings. More woodland than the central basin but never a solid dark forest carpet; occasional small low ridges toward the bottom and right. Leave open ground for the river city and local valley sect. No glowing herbs, resource piles or magical symbols.'),
 '33':('东南盐泽','Southeastern wet ravines, river-fed lowlands and old saline marsh patches. Guide stream runs from its upper-edge entry around x14%, via x25% y22% and x34% y46% toward a spring/wetland headwater near x49% y73%. Keep the water connected along that shape; add only tiny shallow feeder threads around the lower headwater. Pale silver-grey salt-wet soil patches near the middle-right, muted olive reeds and sparse low woodland, grey-brown low hills near lower and right portions. It is part of BAICHUAN river country, not a scorched demon wasteland, desert or snowy tundra. Leave clear sites for the southeastern sect and city, without painting them.'),
}
common='''Create ONE ORIGINAL SQUARE terrain background tile for the BAICHUAN cultivation-game region, one tile of a continuous 3-by-3 map, not a complete self-contained landscape. Target native 2048x2048 or the largest native square output; no dimensions printed.
Accepted style: sparse FLAT antique game-map line-and-wash. Thin dry grey-brown contour lines; each small low hill only 3-5 loose arcing fold lines; very pale grey-olive wash; tiny dark muted olive tree marks; neutral light ivory-grey paper with fine QUIET texture. The separate approved style reference is the style authority. No vivid cyan/blue mountains, lush qinglu painting, realistic rock faces, dramatic lighting, clouds, panoramic horizon, ornate scroll painting or giant foreground peaks. Consistent miniature feature scale in every tile. Paper color should be almost neutral warm grey-cream, not saturated orange, yellow or sepia. Approximately 65-75 percent quiet usable ground.
Guide image is GEOGRAPHY ONLY: blue lines identify river centerlines, blue small polygons are lakes, grey lines are low-ridge direction. Do NOT copy the guide's polygon region borders or background colors. Rivers are restrained flat grey-blue with thin subdued banks and a few reeds, not luminous azure ribbons. Shape and edge-entry locations must follow guide. Natural region transitions, no borders framing a tile.
BAICHUAN CHARACTER: connected river valleys, lakes and basins, foothill passes, old marshes and northeast near-sea transitions. Region names do not authorize copying any existing game's geography or landmarks. These are nine natural pieces of ONE region, not nine political realms, islands or differently colored biomes.
Terrain ONLY: absolutely NO buildings, sect gates, cities, boats, bridges, roads, path dashes, circles, stone waypoints, labels, characters, icons, map title, grid, frame, legends, calligraphy, seal, watermark or signature. Future places/paths/UI are separate layers. Preserve plenty of open ground; do not use hill silhouettes to cover major future node sites.
Tile edges must continue naturally and calmly into neighboring terrain. Keep corner and edge paper tone consistent with the style reference. Never decorate each tile with a mountain frame. Neighbor images, when supplied, are BORDER/PALETTE references, not additional tile subjects to copy into this tile.
SPECIFIC TILE: '''
jobs=[]
for c in d['backgroundPlan']['chunks']:
 key=str(c['row']+1)+str(c['col']+1);title,brief=briefs[key]
 guide=OUT/'引导'/f'guide_{key}.png';mod.draw_guide(c['coreRect'],(1152,1152),labels=False,show_routes=False).save(guide)
 prompt=common+c['id']+' '+title+'. '+brief
 (OUT/f'prompt_{key}.txt').write_text(prompt,encoding='utf-8')
 jobs.append({'key':key,'title':title,'guide':str(guide),'destination':str(OUT/f'百川_{key}_{title}_v01.png'),'prompt':prompt,'coreRect':c['coreRect'],'status':'pending'})
(OUT/'制作清单.json').write_text(json.dumps({'region':'百川','grid':[3,3],'style':'简笔灰褐舆图','jobs':jobs},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
print('Prepared nine distinct Baichuan background jobs and clean guides.')
